  "text": "Argentina lost control because they struggled to play out cleanly, then France turned that pressure into decisive attacks. France had 68% of the passes in the early part of this spell, a possession proxy, while Argentina’s exits broke down: Romero misplaced a pass and Otamendi’s attempted long outlet also failed. [[seq:sb:3869685:s137]] [[seq:sb:3869685:s157]] Camavinga and Coman added fresh options, but the before-and-after figures do not show an immediate French takeover following their introduction. [[ev:sb:3869685:2660]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2661]]\n\nThe decisive collapse came later. Mbappé released Kolo Muani into the box, forcing Otamendi into the foul that produced the penalty; Thuram then supplied Mbappé for the equaliser. [[seq:sb:3869685:s162]] [[seq:sb:3869685:s165]] Across that turning point, Argentina’s share of attacking territory fell from 58% to 28%. It was less a continuous loss of possession than a loss of defensive security, with too little attacking threat to push France back. [[ev:sb:3869685:2928]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2987]]",
